[Ruffland Kennels](https://www.rufflandkennels.com/collections/kennels)

Crash-tested performance kennels we use for the van.

Usual arrangement:
  - x2 [Intermediates](https://www.rufflandkennels.com/products/intermediate-kennel) stacked on driver side
  - x1 [Large](https://www.rufflandkennels.com/products/large-kennel) on passenger side with
  - x1 [Medium](https://www.rufflandkennels.com/products/medium-kennel) on top of the large crate

  The Mediums we own have a smaller 24mm holes in 4mm plastic, but website specs have them as 1.375" (1 and 3/8ths inch) on all crates universally. Starting development with these smaller holes to reduce filament consumption.

  Large and Intermediate crates measured to larger 34.5mm hole in 5mm plastic which seems to match closer to specs on website.

  My measurements being smaller are also acceptable regardless, giving some more tolerance. Also specs likely changed since our purchases.
